    "question": "What SPF sunscreen do I actually need, and does a higher number meaningfully protect me more?",
    "summary": "SPF measures how well sunscreen blocks UVB radiation, but the difference between SPF 30 and higher numbers is smaller than most people realize. For most people, SPF 30–50 broad-spectrum sunscreen applied correctly and reapplied regularly provides excellent protection.",
